      "content": "A"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Monetary policy instruments like Repo Rate, Bank Rate, CRR, and SLR are controlled by the central bank (RBI) to regulate money supply and liquidity.",
        "Fiscal Deficit measures total government expenditure exceeding total receipts excluding borrowings, while Primary Deficit deducts interest payments from the fiscal deficit.",
        "Taxation is categorized into Direct Tax (where burden cannot be shifted) and Indirect Tax (where burden can be shifted).",
        "A loan is classified as a Non-Performing Asset (NPA) if it is not repaid for 90 days.",
        "Stagflation represents a severe macroeconomic scenario characterized by simultaneous inflation and unemployment."
      ],
      "id": "oehqrkb"
    },
